<header><h1>The Nomad: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/F_nomad">The Nomad</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2 id="the-company"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Faction_Abilities:~:text=The%20Company">The Company</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="future-sight"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Future%20Sight">Future Sight</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Nomad player may only predict agenda outcomes via game effects that allow them to do so, e.g. rider action cards.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When can a player make a prediction for the Nomad&rsquo;s Future Sight?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Only when an ability lets you predict, usually a rider.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Nomad player predicts multiple different outcomes, and one of those outcomes is resolved, they will gain the trade good.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If the Nomad player predicts an outcome and votes for another outcome (via the <a href="/F_xxcha">Xxcha</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note), and one of those outcomes is resolved, they will gain the trade good.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Deadly%20Plot"><i>Deadly Plot</i></a> action card is played, the Nomad will not gain a trade good from <sc>Future Sight</sc>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;What is the interaction between Deadly Plot and prediction abilities, given that Deadly Plot specifically says &lsquo;resolved with no effect&rsquo;. A: &lsquo;Resolved with no effect&rsquo; is not an outcome that could have been predicted, so no prediction abilities can trigger.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="the-cavalry"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=The%20Cavalry">The Cavalry</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>One ship is chosen. That ship retains the flagship&rsquo;s values and abilities until it is destroyed or the combat ends.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the chosen ship does not usually have the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability, and is damaged during combat, it will remain damaged even after losing the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>The damaged ship may be chosen again if <i>The Cavalry</i> is played by the same player during a future combat, regaining the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability. As it is already damaged, it will be unable to use its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability again.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>The damaged ship will be repaired during the status phase, regardless of if it currently has the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>In a future combat, the damaged ship may be repaired by the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Duranium_Armor"><i>Duranium Armor</i></a> technology. It will be unable to be damaged again unless it has regained the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Emergency%20Repairs"><i>Emergency Repairs</i></a> action card is played, the damaged ship will not be repaired unless it currently has the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="temporal-command-suite"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Temporal%20Command%20Suite">Temporal Command Suite</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Nomad player may perform a transaction with another player without being neighbors with that player.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Nomad player may perform a transaction with another player even if neither player is the active player.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li><i>Temporal Command Suite</i> may allow the Nomad player to perform a transaction at a time they usually could not. For example, if the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player exhausts their agent, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Leaders:~:text=Suffi%20An">Suffi An</a>, during the strategy phase when another player gains the trade goods on the strategy card they chose, the Nomad player may use <i>Temporal Command Suite</i> and then perform a transaction with the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li><i>Temporal Command Suite</i> may allow the Nomad player to perform a second transaction with another player during one turn.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Nomad&rsquo;s Temporal Command Suite faction technology bypass transaction limits? A: Yes, Temporal Command Suite&rsquo;s transaction does not affect performing a second transaction with the same player that turn.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="memoria"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Flagship:~:text=Memoria">Memoria</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Only the <i>Memoria</i> is adjacent to systems with a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Mech:~:text=Quantum%20Manipulator">Quantum Manipulator</a>. Other ships cannot move between the <i>Memoria</i>&rsquo;s system and a system containing a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Mech:~:text=Quantum%20Manipulator">Quantum Manipulator</a> using this ability.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Other players cannot use the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/PDS#Upgraded_Unit:~:text=Deep%20Space%20Cannon"><sc>Deep Space Cannon</sc></a> ability of units in the same system as a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Mech:~:text=Quantum%20Manipulator">Quantum Manipulator</a> against the <i>Memoria</i>, unless those units are adjacent using another adjacency method.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <i>Memoria</i> cannot retreat to a system containing a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Mech:~:text=Quantum%20Manipulator">Quantum Manipulator</a>, unless it is adjacent to that system using another adjacency method.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 78.7b: &ldquo;To retreat, a player takes all of their ships with a move value in the combat and moves them to a single system that is adjacent to the active system.&rdquo; The retreat destination must be a system adjacent to the active system; the Memoria&rsquo;s ability makes only the ship adjacent to mech systems, not its system.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Intimidate%20Council"><i>Intimidate Council</i></a> objective requires the system to be adjacent to <a href="/R_mecatol_rex">Mecatol Rex</a>. As such, the Nomad player cannot use the <i>Memoria</i>&rsquo;s ability to score this objective. A similar prohibition applies to the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition_4:~:text=Learn%20the%20Secrets%20of%20the%20Cosmos"><i>Learn the Secrets of the Cosmos</i></a> and <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition_4:~:text=Threaten%20Enemies"><i>Threaten Enemies</i></a> objectives.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do ships in Mecatol Rex&rsquo;s system, or in an anomaly, count as adjacent to it for objectives?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Intimidate Council needs ships in two different systems next to Mecatol Rex.&rdquo; The objective needs the systems to be adjacent, not the ships; the Memoria&rsquo;s ability makes only the ship adjacent to mech systems.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <i>Memoria</i> is adjacent to the system that the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Mech:~:text=Quantum%20Manipulator">Quantum Manipulator</a> is in before movement, regardless of if that <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Mech:~:text=Quantum%20Manipulator">Quantum Manipulator</a> is transported during that movement.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="artuno-the-betrayer"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Leaders:~:text=Artuno%20the%20Betrayer">Artuno the Betrayer</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Nomad player would gain trade goods from multiple effects, they may only put the trade goods from one of those effects on Artuno the Betrayer.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>For example, if the Nomad player successfully predicts the outcome of an agenda via the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Trade%20Rider"><i>Trade Rider</i></a> action card, they could put either the trade goods gained from the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Trade%20Rider"><i>Trade Rider</i></a>, or from <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Future%20Sight"><sc>Future Sight</sc></a>, but not both.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>When a player gains trade goods that were on a strategy card, they do not gain them from the supply.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Which trade good gains count for the Nomad agent Artuno?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Trade goods gained from the supply, from action cards, agendas, the Trade card or exploration. Converting commodities doesn&rsquo;t count, and as written neither do trade goods taken off strategy cards.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the Nomad player gains trade goods that were on Artuno the Betrayer, they do not gain them from the supply.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> Same entry: trade goods taken from a card are not counted.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Converting commodities to trade goods is not gaining trade goods from the supply, and does not trigger Artuno the Betrayer.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Which trade good gains count for the Nomad agent Artuno?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Trade goods gained from the supply, from action cards, agendas, the Trade card or exploration. Converting commodities doesn&rsquo;t count, and as written neither do trade goods taken off strategy cards.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="field-marshal-mercer"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Leaders:~:text=Field%20Marshal%20Mercer">Field Marshal Mercer</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The ground forces may be from a system with that player&rsquo;s command token in it.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The ground forces may be on a planet or in a space area.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The ground forces may be removed from different systems.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The ground forces may be placed on one or two planets.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Any damaged mechs remain damaged.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired or does it remain damaged. A: If it is being removed and placed via an ability such as Transit Diodes it stays in the same state.&rdquo; Field Marshal Mercer removes and places ground forces the same way Transit Diodes does.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="the-thundarian"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Leaders:~:text=The%20Thundarian">The Thundarian</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Thundarian may be used during a combat that the Nomad player is not participating in.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can the Nomad agent be used in combats the Nomad aren&rsquo;t in?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; it has no participation requirement.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The dice are rerolled in the same round. Any effects that apply for a single round of combat remain in effect.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>This includes the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Magen_Defense_Grid"><i>Magen Defense Grid</i></a> technology, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Fighter%20Prototype"><i>Fighter Prototype</i></a> and <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Morale%20Boost"><i>Morale Boost</i></a> action cards, the <a href="/F_letnev">Letnev</a> <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Barony_of_Letnev#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Munitions%20Reserves"><sc>Munitions Reserves</sc></a> faction ability, the <a href="/F_naaz_rokha">Naaz&ndash;Rokha</a> <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Naaz-Rokha_Alliance#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Supercharge"><i>Supercharge</i></a> faction technology, the <a href="/F_letnev">Letnev</a> <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Barony_of_Letnev#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=War%20Funding"><i>War Funding</i></a> promissory note, the <a href="/F_letnev">Letnev</a> agent, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Barony_of_Letnev#Leaders:~:text=Viscount%20Unlenn">Viscount Unlenn</a>, and the <a href="/F_sol">Sol</a> agent, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Federation_of_Sol#Leaders:~:text=Evelyn%20DeLouis">Evelyn DeLouis</a>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The <b>Roll Dice</b> step occurs after the start of a round of combat. Any effects that may be played at the start or end of a round of combat cannot be played until the next round of combat.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>This includes the ability of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Duranium_Armor"><i>Duranium Armor</i></a> or <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Magen_Defense_Grid"><i>Magen Defense Grid</i></a> technologies, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Fighter%20Prototype"><i>Fighter Prototype</i></a> or <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Morale%20Boost"><i>Morale Boost</i></a> action cards, the <a href="/F_lizix">L1Z1X</a> <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Harrow"><sc>Harrow</sc></a> or the <a href="/F_letnev">Letnev</a> <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Barony_of_Letnev#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Munitions%20Reserves"><sc>Munitions Reserves</sc></a> faction abilities, the <a href="/F_naaz_rokha">Naaz&ndash;Rokha</a> <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Naaz-Rokha_Alliance#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Supercharge"><i>Supercharge</i></a> faction technology, the <a href="/F_letnev">Letnev</a> <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Barony_of_Letnev#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=War%20Funding"><i>War Funding</i></a> promissory note, the <a href="/F_letnev">Letnev</a> flagship, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Barony_of_Letnev#Flagship:~:text=Arc%20Secundus"><i>Arc Secundus</i></a>, the <a href="/F_letnev">Letnev</a> mech, a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Barony_of_Letnev#Mech:~:text=Dunlain%20Reaper"><i>Dunlain Reaper</i></a>, the <a href="/F_norr">N&rsquo;orr</a> <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Sardakk_N&#x27;orr#:~:text=Exotrireme"><i>Exotrireme II</i></a> dreadnought ability, the <a href="/F_keleres">Keleres</a> <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Council_Keleres#Leaders:~:text=Overwing%20Zeta"><i>Overwing Zeta</i></a> hero ability, the <a href="/F_letnev">Letnev</a> agent, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Barony_of_Letnev#Leaders:~:text=Viscount%20Unlenn">Viscount Unlenn</a>, or the <a href="/F_sol">Sol</a> agent, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Federation_of_Sol#Leaders:~:text=Evelyn%20DeLouis">Evelyn DeLouis</a>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The Thundarian is played at the end of the &ldquo;Roll Dice&rdquo; step, after effects that occur &ldquo;when/after you roll dice&rdquo; or similar.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If The Thundarian is used after the <a href="/F_hacan">Hacan</a> player has spent trade goods for the ability of their flagship, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Emirates_of_Hacan#Flagship:~:text=Wrath%20of%20Kenara"><i>Wrath of Kenara</i></a>, those trade goods remain spent, but the +1 to combat rolls will not be applied for the subsequent dice rolls. The <a href="/F_hacan">Hacan</a> player may spend trade goods after the subsequent dice roll to use the ability of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Emirates_of_Hacan#Flagship:~:text=Wrath%20of%20Kenara"><i>Wrath of Kenara</i></a> for the new results.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If The Thundarian is used after a player has used the ability of <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=The%20Crown%20of%20Thalnos"><i>The Crown of Thalnos</i></a> relic, any units that did not produce hits and so were destroyed remain destroyed, but the +1 to combat rolls will not be applied for the subsequent dice rolls. That player may use the ability of <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=The%20Crown%20of%20Thalnos"><i>The Crown of Thalnos</i></a> on the subsequent dice roll.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If The Thundarian is used after a player has played the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Fire%20Team"><i>Fire Team</i></a> action card, it will be discarded without effect on the subsequent roll.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If The Thundarian is used after a player has played the <a href="/F_letnev">Letnev</a> <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Barony_of_Letnev#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=War%20Funding"><i>War Funding Ω</i></a> promissory note, it will be returned without effect on the subsequent roll.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the <a href="/F_norr">N&rsquo;orr</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Sardakk_N&#x27;orr#:~:text=Valkyrie%20Particle%20Weave"><i>Valkyrie Particle Weave</i></a> faction technology would produce a hit, that hit is not assigned if The Thundarian is used.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If a game effect readies The Thundarian when it is used, its effect may be applied again at the end of the same round of combat.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="navarch-feng"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Leaders:~:text=Navarch%20Feng">Navarch Feng</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The flagship still has a cost of 8.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>The flagship cannot be produced with abilities that are limited by the cost of units, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Integrated_Economy"><i>Integrated Economy</i></a> technology or the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player&rsquo;s agent, Umbat.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the flagship is chosen for the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Scuttle"><i>Scuttle</i></a> action card, the player gains 8 trade goods.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>The objective elected by the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Classified%20Document%20Leaks"><i>Classified Document Leaks</i></a> agenda is a public objective, not a secret objective. Navarch Feng cannot be unlocked by scoring it.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Classified%20Document%20Leaks"><i>Classified Document Leaks</i></a> agenda is discarded, the elected objective is neither a public objective nor a secret objective. Navarch Feng cannot be unlocked by having scored it.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>Commanders cannot become locked after being unlocked. If the Nomad player has only one scored secret objective, and it is elected by the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Classified%20Document%20Leaks"><i>Classified Document Leaks</i></a> agenda, this will have no effect on Navarch Feng.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="ahksyl-siven"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Leaders:~:text=Ahk-Syl%20Siven">Ahk&ndash;Syl Siven</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Leaders:~:text=Probability%20Matrix">Probability Matrix</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The game round ends after the agenda phase (or the status phase if the custodians token is yet to be removed from <a href="/R_mecatol_rex">Mecatol Rex</a>).<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 40 (Game Round): &ldquo;Players skip the agenda phase during the early portion of each game.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Flagship:~:text=Memoria"><i>Memoria</i></a> may transport ground forces from systems containing one of the Nomad player&rsquo;s command tokens while the ability of Ahk&ndash;Syl Siven is active.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does the Nomad&rsquo;s Hero, Ahk-Syl Siven, allow their flagship to pick up groundforces in systems that contain their tokens? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;With the Nomad hero active, can the Memoria pick up units from systems with Nomad command tokens?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; the hero lets the flagship and the units it transports leave command-token systems.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="quantum-manipulator"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Mech:~:text=Quantum%20Manipulator">Quantum Manipulator</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A Quantum Manipulator may use its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability to cancel any hit produced during combat against the Nomad player&rsquo;s ships, not just hits produced by combat rolls. For example, hits produced by anti&ndash;fighter barrage rolls may be canceled.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Effects which directly destroy a ship cannot be prevented with the ability of a Quantum Manipulator.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>Hits that are produced outside of combat cannot be canceled with the ability of a Quantum Manipulator. For example, hits produced by space cannon rolls cannot be canceled.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>When a Quantum Manipulator uses its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability to cancel a hit produced against a ship, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> and <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Codex_I:~:text=Reflective%20Shielding"><i>Reflective Shielding</i></a> action cards cannot be played, as the Quantum Manipulator is not a ship.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>For the same reason, a Quantum Manipulator may use its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability while the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player&rsquo;s flagship, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Flagship:~:text=Fourth%20Moon"><i>Fourth Moon</i></a>, is in the system.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No numbered source. RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Nomad mechs cancel hits with Quantum Manipulator when the Mentak flagship is present?&rdquo; (graded Best reading, unconfirmed; not used): &ldquo;Yes &mdash; the Mentak flagship stops other players&rsquo; ships using Sustain Damage, and a mech isn&rsquo;t a ship.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>During a space combat, a Quantum Manipulator cannot be repaired by the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Duranium_Armor"><i>Duranium Armor</i></a> technology, as it is not participating in the combat.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does the Duranium Armor technology allow you to repair Nomad Mechs that have used their ability to cancel a hit during space combat? A: No, Duranium Armor only affects units participating (rolling dice) in a combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

